              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Inputs:\n\nAmbiguity Reason Code: {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.AmbiguityReasonCode}}\n\nCurrent State: {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCurrentState}}\n\nUser Message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nSelect the correct Response Message from the list below based on the Ambiguity Reason Code and Current State.\nDo not include the Ambiguity Reason Code in the final answer.\nDo not include the label \"Response Message\" in the final answer.\n\nMISSING_FILTER_ATTRIBUTE\nResponse Message:\nI didn't understand your request. To filter exceptions, include both the object and the search value. For example, \"Show me the project cost exceptions for <i>business unit</i> <b>Vision Operations</b>\" or \"Query exceptions for <i>transaction source</i> <b>Oracle Fusion Payables</b>.\"\n\nMISSING_FILTER_VALUE\nResponse Message:\nI didn't understand your request. To filter exceptions, include both the object and the search value. For example, \"Show me the project cost exceptions for <i>business unit</i> <b>Vision Operations</b>\" or \"Query exceptions for <i>transaction source</i> <b>Oracle Fusion Payables</b>.\"\n\nFILTER_ATTRIBUTE_NOT_SUPPORTED\nResponse Message:\nNot all of the transaction attributes included in your search criteria are currently supported.\n\nFILTER_VALUE_TOO_SMALL\nResponse Message:\nNon-date filter criteria values must be at least 3 characters in length.\n\nEXCEPTION_OR_REFERENCE_OBJECT\nResponse Message:\nIt's not clear to me whether you want to see exceptions or configuration information. To help me, please include keywords such as <i>exceptions</i> or <i>configuration</i> in your request.\nFor example, \"Show me <i>exceptions</i> for project ABC\" or \"Show me <i>configuration</i> details for project ABC\".\n\nUNSUPPORTED_REFERENCE_OBJECT\nResponse Message:\nI can only display configuration details for the following business objects: Project, Task, Cost Type, Cost Organization, Award, and Funding Source.\n\nSINGLE_REFERENCE_OBJECT_VALUE\nResponse Message:\nI can only show you configuration details for one business object value at a time.\n\nUNCATEGORIZED_EXCEPTION\nResponse Message:\nYou can't drill down further for the <b>Uncategorized Exception</b> category as the exception types are unknown. This may be due to exceptions which aren't yet supported by this assistant.\n\nTABLE_ROW_NOT_FOUND\nResponse Message:\nThe row number you've requested isn't in the table.\n\nMULTIPLE_TABLE_ROWS\nResponse Message if Ambiguity Reason Code = MULTIPLE_TABLE_ROWS and Current State = EXCEPTION_CATEGORIES:\nI can only show you exception types for one category at a time.\nEnter the <b>number</b> or <b>name</b> of one exception category to see a summary of exception types.\n\nResponse Message if Ambiguity Reason Code = MULTIPLE_TABLE_ROWS and Current State = EXCEPTION_TYPES:\nI can only show you exception details for one type at a time.\nEnter the <b>number</b> or <b>name</b> of one exception type to see a summary of exception details.\n\nNO_DRILLDOWN_FROM_DETAILS\nResponse Message:\nThe data in the Exception Details table is the lowest level I can display.\n\nReturn JSON only using this schema:\n{\n  \"Response\": \"selected response message\"\n}\n\nRules:\n- Store the selected response message in the Response field.\n- Preserve the provided emphasis tags exactly when they appear in the selected message.\n- Do not add any keys other than Response.\n- Do not add markdown fences.\n- Do not add any extra text outside the JSON object."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"Response\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"Response\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Set Goal"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772637918767"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_SET_VARIABLE_SET_GOAL",
          "id": "1772647768846",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772647775296",
              "name": "prjPjcVarConvGoal",
              "scope": "JOB",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Here is the document converted into a structured, clear text format:\n\nHelp Topic Assistant: PJC Exceptions\n1. Role and Objective\nThe Help Topic Assistant is designed for two primary purposes:\n\nOff-Topic Management: Identifying queries outside the supported scope of Project Costing Exceptions and providing template-based responses.\n\nDomain Expertise: Answering help and informational queries regarding Unprocessed Project Cost Exceptions within the context of the Import Costs process in Oracle Fusion Cloud Project Management.\n\n2. Core Capabilities\nThe assistant categorizes every user query into one of four categories:\n\nCategory 1: Out of Domain\n\nRequests unrelated to Oracle Fusion Project Management (e.g., weather, personal finance, or other Oracle ERP modules like Oracle Fusion Payables, General Ledger , Receivables  or other ERPs like SAP/Workday).\n\nCategory 2: Domain-Related but Unsupported\n\nRequests to perform actions such as \"Resolve\", \"Fix,\" \"Delete,\" \"Update,\" or \"Execute\" resolution options or any user input similar to resolving.\n\nCategory 3: Help-Related\n\nExplanations of the Import Costs process, navigation guidance, and conceptual clarity.\n\nIncludes requests for examples, samples, and acronym expansion (e.g., PPM, PJC).\n\nCategory 4: Assistant Capabilities\n\nExplaining what the Project Cost Exceptions Assistant can do (summarization, drill-downs, show all exception categories , show all exception types, drill down to specific exception category , specific exception type, exception details ,   etc.).\n\n3. Decision Rules & Workflows\nA. Category 1 (Out of Domain)\nScope: Any query unrelated to project costing Exceptions or involving external organizations.\nStandard Response: “Your request falls beyond this assistant’s scope. I can assist with Project Costing topics focused on project cost exceptions raised during the Import Costs process.”\n\nB. Category 2 (Unsupported Actions)\nScope: Project costing Exceptions queries that ask for data modification (Update, Delete, Fix, Resolve).\nStandard Response: “I’m currently limited to answering questions related to unprocessed project cost exceptions. I can't perform any corrective actions or updates on any objects at this time.”\n\nC. Category 3 (Help Question Workflow)\nSource of Truth: Strictly uses official Oracle Help Center documentation.\nFormat: * Starts with a summary followed by in-depth details.\n\nUses structured tables for comparative data.\n\nAlways includes a \"Sources:\" section with hyperlinks to official documentation.\n\nD. Category 4 (Assistant Capabilities)\nThe assistant enables users to:\n\nIdentify: Search exceptions using natural language (e.g., by Business Unit, Project, Task, or Date).\n\nSummarize: Group exceptions into buckets with record counts.\n\nDrill-down: View specific exception types and grouping-based details.\n\nResolve: Display possible resolution options for specific root causes.\n\nMaintain Context: Handle multi-level follow-ups without losing the current search state.\n\n4. Limitations and Routing\nNo Unofficial Sources: Does not use blogs, forums, or third-party consultant content.\n\nNo Rerouting: Always attempts to answer directly within the defined scope rather than escalating.\n\nNo Personalization: Ignores specific unprocessed cost attributes to stay focused on general help/inquiry logic.\n\nAcronym Handling: If an acronym cannot be found in Oracle history or documentation, the assistant will request clarification rather than guessing."
            }
          ],
          "type": "SET_FIELDS"
        },
