        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "Gpt Oss",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Filter Manager"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771231391148"
          },
          "code": "PRJ_PJC_LLM_FILTER_MANAGER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1772640384196",
          "id": "1770994019714",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1770994019715_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "- Role: Convert user natural-language request in user message {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} into explicit JSON filter operations. Be strict and deterministic. Do not guess missing values or attributes.Append user message with {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAOldFiltersApplied}} and {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.PFCAFiltersApplied}} .\n\nExtract business attribute names and values from the user's input while strictly ignoring \"Exception Metadata.\"\nLLM Reasoning- Alongwith user message use the {{$context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_RELEVANCY_CHECKER.$output.Reason}} to understand what kind of filter search criteria user wants  , on which attributeName , attributeValue and what you have to do .\n\nUse both user's input and LLM Reasoning for creating filter criteria.\n\nProceed using the steps below.\n\nRules :-\n\nStrict DATE ranges and values retrieval logic , NEVER skip these  - \n  - Transaction Date range: Output TransactionDateRange is {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvTransactionDateDaysRange}} if it is not empty or NULL ; if empty/NULL or user trying new Transaction Date criteria needs to be derived as per rules listed below.\n  - Project Accounting Date range: Output ProjectAccountingDateRange is {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvProjectAccountingDateDaysRange}}  if not empty or NULL; if empty/NULL or user trying new Project Accounting Date criteria needs to be derived as per rules listed below.\n  -Creation Date Range: Output creationDateRange is {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCreationDateDaysRange}}  if not empty or NULL ;if empty/NULL or user trying new Transaction Date criteria needs to be derived as per rules listed below.\n  -Creation Date Value :  Retrieve the Creation Date attribute value from Creation Date attribute name in {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvFilter}}  if not empty or NULL, if empty/NULL or user trying new Creation Date criteria needs to be derived as per rules listed below.\n-Always check Creation Date Value independently of Creation Date Range. Do not assume one implies the other.\n-Validate “not empty” as: value is defined, not NULL, not an empty string, and not whitespace-only.\n-Creation Date Value is required when Creation Date criteria are involved; it must be retrieved from prjPjcVarConvFilter when available.\n-Clearly separate “Range” vs “Value” logic to avoid accidental omission.\n\n\n\n-Date derivation logic   -  \nBETWEEN operator to be used\nDO NOT use any other operator .Strictly use BETWEEN\nAssume start of time is in year 0001, which will help you understand from which year we are considering to entire duration data.\nUse {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} as currentDate as base for your calculation.As per the currentDate get the week info , month's info , years info.\n       From user input for which date range he wants to see data for the  Date attributeName get the start_date and end_date in DD-MM-YYYY. Get the requested Range Text from user input  (e.g., “last 2 weeks”, “January”, “last 8 months” , \"between 1-jan-2026 to 31-jan-2026\" , \"1-1-2026 to 23-1-2026\").requestedRangeText convert to proper date format range like 02-12-2025 - 17-03-2026 .\n\n     Example- Give data for  <dateAttributeName> of last 2 days\n                         so start_date will be 4-4-2026, end_date 6-4-2026\n                         Attribute Value give as :-  \"BETWEEN 4-4-2026 and 6-4-2026\"\n                      Give data for <dateAttributeName> of January, \n                           so start_date will be 1-1-2026, end_date 31-1-2026\n                          Attribute Value give as :-  \"BETWEEN 1-1-2026 and 31-1-2026\"\n                      Give data for <dateAttributeName> between JAN-1-206 to JAN-22-2026, \n                           so start_date will be 1-1-2026, end_date 21-1-2026\n                          Attribute Value give as :-  \"BETWEEN 1-1-2026 and 21-1-2026\"\n                       \n-Behaviour of Creation Date   - \n1. Priority Hierarchy for Creation Date\n\nHighest Priority: If the user mentions a specific date or range in their input, derive it immediately. Store this in <derivedCreationDateValue> and <derivedCreationDateRange>.\n\nMedium Priority: If the user did not specify a date, check if a value exists in {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvFilter}}.\n\nLowest Priority (Fallback Only): Use the 90-day default ONLY if both of the above are null or empty.\n\n2. Specific Instructions\n\nDirection: You must evaluate the User Input for date references before looking at default variables.\n\nStep A: If a date range is mentioned in the user input (even without an attribute name), assign attributeName = \"creationDate\". Follow date derivation logic to populate <derivedCreationDateValue> and <derivedCreationDateRange>.\n\nStep B: Define the final CreationDate's AttributeValue:\n\nUse <derivedCreationDateValue> if it is NOT null.\n\nELSE, use the value from {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvFilter}} .\n\nELSE (as a final fallback only), use end_date and start_date for last 90 days .\n\nStep C: Define the final creationDateRange:\n\nUse <derivedCreationDateRange> if it is NOT null.\n\nELSE, use {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvCreationDateDaysRange}}.\n\n-Strict Processing Rule -\n Before processing the input, check the following sources. If a string from the user's input matches these, it is NOT an attribute name nor a attribute value and must be ignored:\nException Types: Any substring match found in prjPjcVarConvMessageText (mapped to MessageText).\nException Categories: Any substring match found in prjPjcVarConvMessageRAG (mapped to Exception Category).\n\nA name is only considered a valid AttributeName  if it exists as a key in the prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap.\nStrict Prohibition: Never output \"AttributeName\": \"Exception Category\" or \"AttributeName\": \"Exception Type\" \nReasoning: These fields are metadata used for filtering, not business attributes defined in the mapping schema.\n\nExample:Rate Definition , Project Definition are exception categories NOT business attributes.\n\nExtraction Logic\nIdentify the user's input message.\nFilter out any text that matches the \"Exclusion Rules\" (Exception Category/Type).\nFrom the remaining text, identify pairs of Attribute Names and Attribute Values.\nMap the identified Attribute Name to its corresponding technical name using the prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap.\n\n- {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap}} has data that all attribute names and display value which will help you to get the relevant attributes.Strctly follow this rule.\n\n- Output: Return only a single JSON object with:\n  - operations: array of objects with fields:\n  \n\n\n-If input is having days/week/month range without explicitly giving any AttributeName for which that date range is mentioned like give me exceptions for last 1000 days , last 1 week , last 3 months , 1 week of data, current month of data,  then 'last 1000 days'/ 'last 3 months'/'last 1 week/'1 week'/'current month' is NOT attribute value neither attribute name. Its just a range of days specified  ,user is requesting data for.You need to see attribute name/value  extract them only.\n\n    - AttributeName: It will be input by user in {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}  and must be one of {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap}} ; or an empty string \"\" if not specified.Synonyms in {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap}} will help you get the attributeName user is searching for . Example get exceptions for task description 2.1 , here  task description is synonym for taskName , so taskName is attributeName , attributeValue is 2.1.LLM Reasoning will help to get exact attributeName , attributeValue.\n  By seeing input message map to the attribute name about the attributes. Dont guess attribute names.If you are not able to decide if attribute name gets mapped to name or number , have both name , number in AttributeName like :- only project is given in input, can be project name or project number , in output have both Project Name , Project Number as AttributeNames for same attribute value.\n    - AttributeValue: string or integer , if string enclose each ATTRIBUTE VALUE in ''  (use empty string \"\" for REMOVE and KEEP unless a new value is provided) .If Multiple attribute values are there for same attribute name , put them as comma separated.For attribute names which are yes/no based like Billable , captilizable , invoice without giving explicit value you need to deduce by seeing user input intent like get me data for non - billable exceptions  - So here non-billable is Billable = 'No' , get me data for billable exceptions , Billable = Yes likewise for other yes.no based attributes.\n     - When attributeName is given in user input and it is date related and the attributeName is explicitly mentioned in user input like Transaction Date attribute , project accounting ; then  the date AttributeValue should be derived following date derivation logic.For TransactionDateRange,ProjectAccountingDateRange use DATE ranges retrieval logic if its empty then derive the TransactionDateRange following date derivation logic.\n  -If current period is input , use CreationDate as current month as the attribute and current month being value , using date derivation logic.\n      \n      \n    - Indicator: must be one of ADD, REMOVE, KEEP \n    - errors: optional string; include only when there is an issue specific to this operation. If no issue, omit this field.\n- Action detection (even if the user does not say “filter” or “search”):\n  - ADD when user says or implies: apply, add, append, include, set, filter by, search for, results for, show, find, give results for\n  - REMOVE when user says or implies: remove, clear, delete, drop, exclude for attributes like remove/clear batch and creation date , so REMOVE should be used for costBatch and creationDate attributes.\n  - KEEP when user says or implies: keep applied, keep, leave as is\n\n\n\n\n1)General inquiries with no attribute and no value:\n -Setup related enquiries, User input will have SETUP keyword and will suggest that user is trying to know about setup , so treat as general enquiry.\n  -Always apply behaviour of creationDate filter.\n  - If the input is a generic request that does not specify any recognisable attribute and does not provide any attribute value (e.g., “give details”, “show all details”, “show all the exceptions” , \"give me exceptions for last 300 days \" , \"\"give me exceptions for last 1 week\"\").In this case the input contains neither a recognizable attribute NOR any potential attribute value. If any non-empty value text is present (that is not days/weeks/months and not part of MessageText/MessageRAG), do NOT treat as general inquiry.\n-General enquire can be  also a case when user just inputs a serial number to see details of table row - this is also general enquiry like 1 ,show 1 , give details of 2 , give details of serial number 3 etc.For this check the {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} and see before the current user input {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} , previous agent response was a table related to exception category or exception Type or exception details  is displayed and user is responding to it.\nreturn:\n    {\n      {\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n  ]\n}\n    }\n\n   Remove all user intent is different and given below should not be clubbed with this.\n- Multiple actions in a single request are supported.\n- Preserve user-provided value casing; trim leading and trailing spaces.\n\n\n2) No inference rules:\n  - If the input includes any value-like token(s) but no valid attribute from DisplaytoAttributeMap, output an ADD with AttributeName = '' and include errors as ‘No attribute name provided for value ‘<value>’\".Any non-empty text following intents such as ‘for’, ‘of’, ‘with’, ‘=’, ‘is’, ‘named’, or quoted text is considered a potential value unless it matches MessageText or MessageRAG, or is a pure date-range duration (days/weeks/months).If the input matches the pattern: ‘give/show/get … details (for|of) <value>’ and no attribute from DisplaytoAttributeMap is present do not attempt to infer an attribute name from the value; leave AttributeName empty.If ADD is requested without a value (for example, “add project number”), create an operation with AttributeName = \"projectNumber\", AttributeValue = \"\", Indicator = \"ADD\", and set errors = \"ADD requested for projectNumber but no value provided\".\n\n-If ADD is requested without a value (for example, “add project number”), create an operation with AttributeName = \"projectNumber\", AttributeValue = \"\", Indicator = \"ADD\", and set errors = \"ADD requested for projectNumber but no value provided\".\n\n3)Special cases:\n  - For  \"Start Over\" , \"Get all Exceptions\",\"Get All Exceptions\" , \"get all exceptions\",\"reset\",“remove all”, “clear all filters”, or “remove all applied search criteria”, output REMOVE for all known attributes.All known attribute names are in {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap}} .Creation date default to last 90 days.\n    [\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"job\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" }\n      .......\n     { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"BETWEEN 6-1-2026 and 6-4-2026\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n    ]\n    Do not include errors fields for these operations.\n- Output only the JSON object, no extra text.\n\n4) When REMOVE is specifically given for Creation Date , that time add indicator as REMOVE for creation date\n   Example: remove creation date filter \n   { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\",  \"AttributeValue\": \"\",\"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" }\n\n\nDisplayLabel will be the displayValue from  {{$context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvDisplaytoAttributeMap}} for the corresponding attributeName.\nIf AttributeName has Name and Number both for a entity like projectName , projectNumber both are present in AttributeName , then displayValue put only the base entity (which is without Name or Number) for Project Name, Project Number will be Project.Similarly do for other Name/Number attributes like TaskName/ TaskNumber , AwardName/AwardNumber.\n\nExamples\n\nCreationDateattributeValue can be default or whatever user gives\nInput: give details\nOutput:\n{\n   { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n}\n\n\n\nInput: show all the exceptions\nCreationDateattributeValue will be for last 90 days , PUT REMOVE for all search attributes except creationDate\nOutput:\n   [\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"job\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" }\n      .......\n     { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"BETWEEN 6-1-2026 and 6-4-2026\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n    ]\n\nInput: Get all exceptions\nCreationDateattributeValue will be for last 90 days , PUT REMOVE for all  other search attributes except creationDate\nOutput:\n   [\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"job\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" }\n      .......\n     { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"BETWEEN 6-1-2026 and 6-4-2026\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n    ]\n\nInput: Start Over\nCreationDateattributeValue will be for last 90 days , PUT REMOVE for all search attributes except creationDate\nOutput:\n   [\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n      { \"AttributeName\": \"job\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" }\n      .......\n     { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"BETWEEN 6-1-2026 and 6-4-2026\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n    ]\n\n\n\nInput: show all the exceptions for last 6 months\nOutput:\n{\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n}\n\nInput: show all the exceptions for Transaction Date of last 2 weeks\nOutput:\n{\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" } ,     { \"AttributeName\": \"TransactionDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'BETWEEN 24-3-2026 and 6-4-2026'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n}\n\nInput: give results for PROJECT NUMBER ZCVT-YU\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'ZCVT-YU'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" },{ \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n  ]\n}\nInput: give results for PROJECT ZCVT-YU\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber, projectName\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'ZCVT-YU'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" },{ \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: give results for PROJECT NUMBERS ZCVT-YU , ZCVT-YX\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'ZCVT-YU' , ' ZCVT-YX'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" },{ \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: I want to see results for PROJECT NUMBER ZCVT-YU\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'ZCVT-YU'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" },{ \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": CreationDateattributeValue, \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: I want to see details for Person NUMBER ZCVT-YU\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"personNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'ZCVT-YU'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" },{ \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\":CreationDateattributeValue\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: i want to remove  task number , project number and creation date\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\"}\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"creationDate\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: i want to remove filter criteria task number , add project number\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\", \"errors\": \"ADD requested for projectNumber but no value provided\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: I want to remove search criteria task, job , and keep project applied\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"job\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"KEEP\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: remove all applied search criteria\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"projectNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"taskNumber\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" },\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"job\", \"AttributeValue\": \"\", \"Indicator\": \"REMOVE\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: give results for Smith\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"\", \"AttributeValue\": \"Smith\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\", \"errors\": \"No attribute name provided for value 'Smith'\" }\n  ]\n}\n\nInput: give details for Smith\nOutput:\n{\n  \"operations\": [\n    { \"AttributeName\": \"\", \"AttributeValue\": \"'Smith'\", \"Indicator\": \"ADD\", \"errors\": \"No attribute name provided for value 'Smith'\" }\n  ]\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n\n        \"CreationDateFilterReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Operations\": {\n            \"type\": \"array\",\n            \"items\": {\n                \"type\": \"object\",\n                \"properties\": {                               \n\n                                \"AttributeName\": {\n                                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                               },\n                                \"AttributeValue\": {\n                                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                               },\n                                \"DisplayLabel\": {\n                                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                               },\n                                \"Indicator\": {\n                                        \"type\": \"string\"\n                               }\n\n\n\n}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Filter Array Preparation",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "// 1. Data Assignment\nvar existingData = $context.$variables.prjPjcVarConvFilter;\nvar opsData = $context.$nodes.PRJ_PJC_LLM_FILTER_MANAGER.$output;\n\n// 2. Normalize Data & Skip specific error string\nvar existingFilters = [];\nif (existingData && existingData.Filter) {\n    var rawFilters = Array.isArray(existingData.Filter) ? existingData.Filter : [existingData.Filter];\n    existingFilters = rawFilters.filter(function(item) {\n        return typeof item === 'object' && item !== null;\n    });\n}\n\n// 3. Handle casing for \"operations\" vs \"Operations\"\nvar operations = (opsData && (opsData.Operations || opsData.operations)) ? (opsData.Operations || opsData.operations) : [];\n\nvar finalFilters = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(existingFilters)); \nvar outputValue = null;\n\n// 4. Logic & Validation Block\nif (operations.length === 0) {\n    outputValue = finalFilters;\n} else {\n    var hasError = false;\n    for (var i = 0; i < operations.length; i++) {\n        var op = operations[i];\n        if (op.Error || op.error || op.Errors || op.errors) {\n            hasError = true;\n            break;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (hasError) {\n        outputValue = \"Filter criteria cant be formed\";\n    } else {\n        // 5. Processing Phase\n        for (var j = 0; j < operations.length; j++) {\n            var op = operations[j];\n            var attr = (op.AttributeName || \"\").trim();\n            var val = op.AttributeValue;\n            var label = op.DisplayLabel || \"\"; // New: Extract DisplayLabel\n            var indicator = (op.Indicator || op.indicator || \"\").toUpperCase();\n\n            if (indicator === \"ADD\") {\n                var found = false;\n                for (var k = 0; k < finalFilters.length; k++) {\n                    // Update existing filter with new value and label\n                    if (finalFilters[k].AttributeName === attr) {\n                        finalFilters[k].AttributeValue = val; \n                        finalFilters[k].DisplayLabel = label; // Update Label\n                        found = true;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (!found) {\n                    // Push new filter with Label\n                    finalFilters.push({ \n                        \"AttributeName\": attr, \n                        \"AttributeValue\": val, \n                        \"DisplayLabel\": label \n                    });\n                }\n            } else if (indicator === \"REMOVE\") {\n                // Multi-Attribute Remove Logic\n                finalFilters = finalFilters.filter(function(item) {\n                    var existingAttr = (item.AttributeName || \"\");\n                    var attrParts = existingAttr.split(\",\").map(function(s) { return s.trim(); });\n                    return attrParts.indexOf(attr) === -1;\n                });\n            }\n        }\n        outputValue = finalFilters;\n    }\n}\n\n// 6. Final Output Structure\nvar result = {\n    \"Filter\": outputValue\n};\n\nreturn JSON.stringify(result);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1771583084121"
